{
 "artist": "Frederic Remington",
 "slug": "frederic-remington",
 "born": 1861,
 "died": 1909,
 "nationality": "American",
 "facts": [
  {
   "text": "Remington signed his paintings and drawings with his full name, 'Frederic Remington', often in capitals with a long flourish before and after.",
   "source": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/97908",
   "source_name": "Art Institute of Chicago"
  },
  {
   "text": "Some paintings made for reproduction carry a copyright notice beside the signature, such as 'Copyright 1890 / By / Frederic Remington' on A Mexican Vaquero and 'Copyrighted / Frederic Remington / '89' on The Mexican Major.",
   "source": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/97907",
   "source_name": "Art Institute of Chicago"
  },
  {
   "text": "He also signed and dated pen-and-ink illustrations, for example 'Frederic Remington 1889' on On the Bridle Path, Central Park.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.185008.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "His bronzes are signed in the cast, usually 'Frederic Remington' on the base, often with 'Copyright' or 'Copyrighted' and the founder's mark; on one cast of The Bronco Buster a '55' is worked into the F of the signature.",
   "source": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/97916",
   "source_name": "Art Institute of Chicago"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Frederic Remington catalogue raisonné records each work's signature and inscriptions by position, and notes copyright only where a record from his lifetime was found.",
   "source": "https://centerofthewest.org/catalogs/remington/",
   "source_name": "Buffalo Bill Center of the West"
  }
 ],
